From c0a24f1252641a3d520281f69ac3d62bedee7560 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:24:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-118354: Improper input validation in Skia

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1395157:
Treat VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN as VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST

We normally would not expect VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN as this means there is
either a problem with our calls to Vulkan which wasn't caught with
validation layers, or the driver has an implementation issue. Since it
is not normally expected and is unclear what the issue is we will treat
is as a device lost.

Bug: 568936430
Change-Id: I87a145a418fd41a2e6d513ca1a7525556a55c3db
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1395157
Commit-Queue: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Reviewed-on: https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtwebengine-chromium/+/784485
Reviewed-by: Michal Klocek <michal.klocek@qt.io>
